  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00002"><title>Cool Down Activity</title><exercise id="_650e2f67-e71c-4963-8f3e-5322c96c2458" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00001"><para id="para-00001">1. Which of these polynomials has a greatest common factor of 1?</para><para id="para-00002">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00003">\(10q^2 + 14q + 20\)</para><para id="para-00004">\(12x^3 − 2x\)</para><para id="para-00005">\(12x^3y − 7g^8h^3 + 11s^2\)</para><para id="para-00006">\(-2x-4\)</para></problem><solution id="sol-00001"><para id="para-00007">Correct! \(12x^3y − 7g^8h^3 + 11s^2\)</para><para id="para-00008">Try again. Check to see if \(2\) is a factor in each term in the expression.</para></solution></exercise></section><para id="para-00009">Determine if the expression can be factored by grouping. If it can, factor the expression. If not, answer “prime.”</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00001">
  <problem id="prob-00002">
    <para id="para-00010">\(cd + 6c + 4d + 24\)</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00002">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00011">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00012">\((d + 6)(c + 4)\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00002">
  <problem id="prob-00003">
    <para id="para-00013">\(x^2 − y + 4w − 3\)</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00003">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00014">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00015">prime</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
